Notes
================================================================================
• Talking to it is not modifying it: writing your own program, bot or game that
  calls the DiceCore HTTP API creates a separate work, not a derivative of
  DiceCore, and this license places no conditions on that program.
• Your data is yours: images you capture, datasets you collect and models you
  train with DiceCore belong to you and are not covered by this license.
• Commercial licensing requires the prior separate written permission of the
  copyright holder.
• Third-party components: DiceCore builds on third-party software (for example
  OpenCV, numpy, FastAPI, uvicorn, onnxruntime and PyTorch) licensed under their
  own separate terms. This license applies only to the original DiceCore material
  created by the copyright holder and does not modify or supersede those
  third-party licenses.
• No warranty: THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND.
  DiceCore reports what it believes it sees, and it will sometimes be wrong. Do
  not use it where a wrong number matters — for money, for wagers, or as a
  referee no one can overrule. To the maximum extent permitted by law, the
  copyright holder is not liable for any claim, damages, or other liability
  arising from the software or its use.
• Cameras and privacy: DiceCore runs entirely on your own network and sends
  nothing anywhere. A camera pointed at a table still films the room around it,
  and recording people may require their consent where you live. It is YOUR
  responsibility to check and comply with the applicable law before pointing a
  camera at anything.
